    "details": "The OpenVoxProject reports:\n\n> The Puppet/OpenVox report is a JSON document the agent sends to the\n> server after each enforcement run. It details what changes were made,\n> any warnings or error messages, and any resources that failed to apply\n> correctly. It also contains a full list of all events that happened,\n> where an event might be \"content \\<foo\\> changed to \\<bar\\>\" or the\n> like. In some circumstances involving custom resource types, an event\n> might include a serialized Ruby object (programming code turned into\n> text) instead of just plain JSON. When the report is processed, these\n> objects are deserialized back into something the compiler can use.\n> Unfortunately a malicious event object can be constructed in such a\n> way that code executes on the server when this happens.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0599",
